<title>USA: IGA Inc to add 35 supermarkets in China.</title>
<headline>IGA Inc to add 35 supermarkets in China.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>IGA Inc, an alliance of supermarkets, said it would open 35 additional stores in China.</p>
<p>IGA now has 62 stores in China with annual sales of more than $100 million, up from $9 million a year ago.</p>
<p>Two years ago, IGA became the first U.S. grocer to enter the Chinese market, the company said.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
